# thoth_policy_bundle

Manages versioned OPA/Cedar policy bundles for runtime sidecar enforcement.

~> **A change made with an API key is pending until a person approves it.** Create, update and destroy made with an
API key (or a service or system principal) are recorded and wait for a signed-in org admin with a second factor to
approve them; the bundles agents are held to do not change meanwhile. `terraform apply` then stops with "Policy bundle
change is pending approval" and the change id, and **`terraform plan` keeps showing the change** (nothing is saved in
state, so it never reports "no changes" while the old bundle is still enforced). An org admin lists pending changes with
`GET /<tenant>/thoth/policy-bundle-changes`, reads one with `GET .../<change id>`, and approves or rejects it with `POST
.../approve` or `.../reject` (an approval must send the `content_hash` it read, or it is refused); the admin who owns the key cannot approve it unless the audited single-admin
self-approval setting is on, and a change expires after 14 days. After approval, run `terraform apply` again: it
returns the approved bundle and saves its id without publishing a copy (after an approved destroy, run `terraform
destroy` again). The dashboard, `thothctl` and MCP do not reach these routes yet. A change made with a signed-in
`thothctl` session applies at once.

## Example Usage

```hcl
resource "thoth_policy_bundle" "standard_dlp_opa" {
  name        = "standard-dlp"
  description = "Customer-agnostic purpose/sensitivity DLP baseline"
  framework   = "OPA"
  raw_policy  = file("${path.module}/policies/opa-standard-dlp.rego")
  enforcement_mode = "enforce"
}

resource "thoth_policy_bundle" "least_privilege_cedar" {
  name        = "least-privilege-analyst"
  description = "Tier-targeted least-privilege baseline"
  framework   = "CEDAR"
  raw_policy  = file("${path.module}/policies/cedar-least-privilege-analyst.cedar")
  assignments = ["agent:security-analyst-agent", "agent:coding-agent"]
  enforcement_mode = "enforce"
}

resource "thoth_policy_bundle" "enterprise_standard" {
  name          = "global-governance"
  framework     = "OPA"
  source_uri    = "s3://atensec-governance-us-west-2/v2.4.1/standard.rego"
  s3_version_id = "3Lg....optionalVersionId"
  expected_hash = "sha256:e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"
  assignments   = ["all"]
  enforcement_mode = "enforce"
}

resource "thoth_policy_bundle" "pilot_local_file" {
  name        = "pilot-dev-local"
  framework   = "OPA"
  source_uri  = "file:///etc/thoth/policies/pilot.rego"
  enforcement_mode = "observe"
}
```

